{%- comment -%}
  PG Save Badge: make the SAVE % badge on every offer tile the first thing read.

  pg-theme-css draws it small and dark:

      .pgx-lad-badge{font-size:11.5px;font-weight:800;padding:5px 14px;
                     background:#0D0714;color:#fff;border:1px solid rgba(139,68,190,.6)}

  On a near-black tile on a near-black page that is a dark pill on a dark card —
  the number a shopper is meant to see first is the quietest thing in the tile.
  It now carries the same purple gradient as the add-to-cart buttons, at a
  larger size and heavier weight, so the saving reads before the price does.

  One rule covers every tile on every product: pgLadder's ladder tiles, pgDuo's
  Duo Pack ([data-pg-duosave]) and pg-landing's single tile
  ([data-pg-singlesave]) all render the badge with this class.

  Registered in sections/header-group.json, which renders before pg-theme-css in
  the footer group — so these are stamped !important and id-scoped to outrank it
  on specificity rather than on source order.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  html body #pgx .pgx-lad-badge{
    background:linear-gradient(120deg,#B478E0 0%,#9B4BC4 40%,#7A2FA2 100%) !important;
    color:#FFFFFF !important;
    font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif !important;
    font-size:14px !important;
    font-weight:900 !important;
    letter-spacing:.05em !important;
    padding:7px 17px !important;
    border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.38) !important;
    box-shadow:0 12px 26px -12px rgba(139,68,190,.95) !important;
    text-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.35) !important;
    text-transform:uppercase !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
  }
  @media (max-width:600px){
    html body #pgx .pgx-lad-badge{font-size:13px !important;padding:6px 14px !important}
  }
</style>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Save Badge", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG Save Badge"}]}
{% endschema %}
